      "writtenOn": "2025-08-09T19:46:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m OK with adding new legacy EC tests from a coverage point of view. You may find this framework challenging to work with. You might find it slightly more convenient to write tests in the Zephyr framework similar to the `usb_hard_reset` [tests](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/test/drivers/default/src/integration/usbc/usb_hard_reset.c). These are among our older Zephyr tests, so they\u0027re not super polished, e.g. checking the reported TC state directly via an internal function rather than using a host command or the TCPC registers. But they do have access to the Zephyr test framework. Just a thought.",
      "revId": "67872f40970a4c09eef0e312a2e6a8fd78e251dc",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
